SUMMARY:80's Summer Movie Series
DESCRIPTION:Step back into the 80s! To celebrate their 40-year reunion\, the Montclair High School Class of 1986 is bringing four classic films back to the big screen at the historic Bellevue Theatre. \nThe Lineup (Sundays at 2:30 PM / Doors at 2:00 PM): \nJuly 26: Trading Places\nAugust 9: Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom\nAugust 30: Footloose\nSeptember 13: Ferris Bueller’s Day Off \nThe Cause: Proceeds support the MHS Class of 1986 Scholarship\, administered through the Montclair Scholarship Fund. Created entirely through alumni donations\, the Class of 1986 is proudly one of only two MHS graduating classes to establish a named\, class-specific scholarship\, supporting graduating Mounties for more than a decade. \nTickets: $30 (includes popcorn!). Note: Seating is limited\, and tickets must be purchased in advance online—none will be sold at the door. Ticket holders also score special local perks from Applegate Farm\, Tinga’s Fresh Mexican BBQ\, The Grape Collective\, Tino’s Artisan Pizza Co.\, and The General Store. \nFor event details\, to purchase tickets\, or make a donation\, click the link or scan the QR code! MHSMovieSeries2.eventbrite.com \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/80s-summer-movie-series/2026-08-09/
LOCATION:Bellevue Theatre\, 260 Bellevue Avenue\, Upper Montclair\, 07043\, United States
CATEGORIES:Film
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/80s-Movie-Poster-8.5x14.png
